1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:01,964
If your empire is so
evil,

2
00:00:01,984 --> 00:00:04,060
why hasn't everyone
rebelled?

3
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:05,983
Ask the people
holding it up.

4
00:00:06,003 --> 00:00:07,584
The farmer gets safe
roads,

5
00:00:07,604 --> 00:00:09,197
and bread every
winter.

6
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:11,036
The clerk remembers
the chaos before the

7
00:00:11,056 --> 00:00:11,882
throne.

8
00:00:11,902 --> 00:00:14,083
The soldier's mother
needs his wage.

9
00:00:14,103 --> 00:00:15,468
The neighbour keeps
quiet.

10
00:00:15,488 --> 00:00:17,578
Complainers get a
knock at night.

11
00:00:17,598 --> 00:00:19,276
And nobody can
picture anything

12
00:00:19,296 --> 00:00:20,289
better.

13
00:00:20,309 --> 00:00:22,569
A villainous empire
is believable when

14
00:00:22,589 --> 00:00:24,720
its supporters
aren't villains.

15
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:26,470
Share this with
someone writing a

16
00:00:26,490 --> 00:00:29,070
one-dimensional
villainous empire.
